<title>USA: U.S. blue chips drift in negative ground, techs up.</title>
<headline>U.S. blue chips drift in negative ground, techs up.</headline>
<text>
<p>The Dow industrials wallowed in negative territory on Monday, taking direction from a weak bond market which was still spooked by rate jitters after strong economic data released Friday. Dow off 38 points at 8157, Nasdaq gains four points to 1598. Long bond down 16/32 to yield 6.49 percent.</p>
